"1. During RT of a 25 mm wall pressure vessel weld (ASME VIII Div.1), the radiographer places the IQI on the source side. The procedure requires source-side IQI placement. The IQI image is visible on the film. However, no shim was placed under the IQI and the IQI is directly on the weld crown. What is the technical concern?",
"The IQI placed directly on the weld crown will produce an artificially better sensitivity reading because the IQI is at a thicker section of the part.\nThe IQI placed on the weld crown is at a raised area; without a shim equal to the weld crown height, the IQI hole image represents a sensitivity level achieved through the weld crown, not through the full 25 mm base metal — the true sensitivity at the base metal section is unverified.\nNo concern — ASME V requires IQI placement on the highest point of the part for worst-case sensitivity assessment.\nThe IQI should be placed on the film side for maximum sensitivity verification.",
"The IQI placed on the weld crown is at a raised area; without a shim equal to the weld crown height, the IQI hole image represents a sensitivity level achieved through the weld crown, not through the full 25 mm base metal — the true sensitivity at the base metal section is unverified.",
"ASME V T-277.1(a): a shim equal to the maximum weld crown height must be placed under the IQI when placed on the crown, so the IQI is exposed through material of the same total thickness as the weld. Without the shim, the IQI is exposed through greater thickness (crown + base), yielding an artificially better (thicker) sensitivity value than the base metal area actually receives.",
