"5. During MT (Magnetic Particle Inspection) of a weld using the continuous method per ASME V Article 7, the technician applies the magnetic particles before the magnetising current is energised, then energises the current. What is the nonconformance?",
"No nonconformance — particles can be applied before or after energising the current per ASME V.\nNonconformance — the continuous method requires the magnetic particles to be applied WHILE the magnetising current is energised; applying particles before magnetisation means the particles are not being drawn to leakage flux at active indication sites.\nNonconformance — the particles must be applied after the current is shut off, not before.\nNo nonconformance — the sequence of particle application relative to current is at the technician's discretion.",
"Nonconformance — the continuous method requires the magnetic particles to be applied WHILE the magnetising current is energised; applying particles before magnetisation means the particles are not being drawn to leakage flux at active indication sites.",
