"19. During eddy current testing (ECT) of heat exchanger tubes, the technician uses a 200 kHz probe. A signal is detected at 40° phase angle and 60% amplitude (relative to calibration notch). In standard heat exchanger ECT lissajous pattern analysis, what does the phase angle indicate?",
"Phase angle of 40° indicates a through-wall hole (100% wall loss).\nPhase angle of 40° is consistent with a volumetric defect (corrosion pit or pitting) in the mid-wall to outer surface region; the phase angle distinguishes through-wall defects (~0°) from ID surface defects (~90°).\nPhase angle of 40° indicates a manufacturing defect in the tube (seam weld).\nPhase angle indicates the depth of the defect as a direct percentage of wall thickness (40° = 40% wall loss).",
