"Over-washing — a 350 kPa spray is excessively aggressive and may have removed penetrant from tight surface cracks; the maximum recommended spray pressure per ASME V T-672.2 is 275 kPa (40 psi); all areas must be re-examined after re-applying penetrant using correct washing pressure.",
"ASME V T-672.2 specifies maximum wash pressure of 275 kPa (40 psi) and maximum water temperature of 43°C (110°F) for water-washable penetrant removal. Excessive pressure washes penetrant from tight, shallow discontinuities — creating false 'clean' results. Any PT result following over-washing may be unreliable and must be repeated.",
